# Sequential focus navigation (HTML §6.6.3, §6.6.5): Tab walks a page's
# focusable areas in the order every engine gives them — positive tabindex
# values first, ascending, then the rest in flat-tree order; a negative
# tabindex, a disabled control, a hidden input, display: none, visibility:
# hidden, a closed details' contents and an inert subtree left out; one
# stop per radio group (the checked button, else the first going forward
# and the last going back); a shadow tree's fields in the host's place with
# the slotted content where its slot is; nested frames entered and left
# both ways; a scroll container with nothing focusable inside a stop of its
# own. Past the page's last stop the focus goes to the toolbar — reload,
# the address bar, the star, the menu — and from its last back into the
# page; Shift+Tab the whole way back. Never a trap.
resize 800 900
open focus-order.html
advance 50 2
assert-focused-id none
key tab
assert-focused-id p1
key tab
assert-focused-id p2
key tab
assert-focused-id l1
key tab
assert-focused-id b1
key tab
assert-focused-id r2
key tab
assert-focused-id h1
key tab
assert-focused-id s1
key tab
assert-focused-id slotted
key tab
assert-focused-id s2
key tab
assert-focused-id fa
key tab
assert-focused-id fi
key tab
assert-focused-id fb
key tab
assert-focused-id scroll
key tab
assert-focused-id sumc
key tab
assert-focused-id sumo
key tab
assert-focused-id unfolded
key tab
assert-focused-id after
key tab
assert-focused-id last
key tab
assert-chrome-focus back
assert-focused-id none
key tab
assert-chrome-focus reload
key tab
assert-chrome-focus address
key tab
assert-chrome-focus star
key tab
assert-chrome-focus reader
key tab
assert-chrome-focus menu
key tab
assert-chrome-focus none
assert-focused-id p1
# And back the whole way: into the toolbar from the page's first stop,
# then from its first stop to the page's last.
key shift+tab
assert-chrome-focus menu
key shift+tab
key shift+tab
key shift+tab
key shift+tab
key shift+tab
assert-chrome-focus back
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id last
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id after
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id unfolded
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id sumo
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id sumc
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id scroll
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id fb
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id fi
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id fa
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id s2
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id slotted
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id s1
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id h2
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id r2
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id b1
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id l1
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id p2
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id p1
key shift+tab
assert-chrome-focus menu

# The sequential focus navigation starting point: a press on text that
# takes no focus is where Tab goes on from, either way; so is the target of
# a move to a fragment, though the link pressed keeps the focus. A page
# that cancels Tab's keydown keeps the focus where it is (a dialog's trap).
open data:text/html,<style>body{margin:8px;font-family:"Sashfold Mono";font-size:16px;line-height:20px}</style><a id=a href=%23t>jump</a><p>middle words</p><a id=b href=%23>b</a><p id=t>target words</p><a id=c href=%23>c</a><a id=d href=%23>d</a><script>document.addEventListener('keydown',function(e){if(e.key==='Tab'&&document.activeElement.id==='d')e.preventDefault()})</script>
click-text middle
assert-focused-id none
key tab
assert-focused-id b
click-text middle
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id a
click-text jump
assert-focused-id a
key tab
assert-focused-id c
key tab
assert-focused-id d
key tab
assert-focused-id d
key shift+tab
assert-focused-id d
